##
    A storefront, spread across folders.

    The 'output' is the reason to notice this is a project rather than a folder. Every loose .pc
    in 'samples' builds into the one 'bin' beside them, because a source file has nowhere to
    record where its build should go — so forty programs fill one folder with forty assemblies.

    A project is a build describing itself, and has somewhere to put the answer. This one keeps
    its build to itself. The path is read from the project file, so it means the same wherever
    the build is started from, and the folder is made if it is not there.
##

project Storefront
    source Program.pc
    source models
    source pricing
    output ../bin/storefront
end project
